  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Place the basil in a blender. Pour in about 1 tablespoon of the oil, and blend basil into a paste. Gradually add pine nuts, Parmesan cheese, garlic, chili powder, and remaining oil. Continue to blend until smooth.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Reader Comments",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Toast your pine nuts first to intensify their nutty flavor (roll around in a very hot pan until lightly browned on some but not all sides), then chop them all in your food processer a bit, but not too much as you want texture.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Add some seasoned salt and red pepper flakes while blending!",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "The chili powder is such a great addition, adding zip but no noticeable flavor.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Less oil has worked fine, as well as fewer pine nuts when short.",
      "group": null
    },
    {
      "text": "TIP: Pesto should not be frozen with the cheese in it; it makes one of the ingredients rancid. Freeze and add cheese later.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
